{
  "_source": "Helen Edgar's own three playlists on her AutisticRealms channel: Faery Yurt’s Yarn (49 rows on 2026-10-18) and Strange things will happen (15 rows, which she asked for in the Music Room the same day), both of which play in the Music Room, and Library Music (18 rows, the same day), which plays on the gramophone in the Reading Room. Each was read off its own page on 2026-10-18, in the playlist's own order (YouTube serves a playlist's rows as lockupViewModel now, which yt-dlp is not installed here to read; each header's count matched the rows served, so nothing was hidden). Every id was then opened on its own watch page that day: all answered OK, family-safe and not live; all but one answered playableInEmbed true, and that one is a door. Each runtime is that page's lengthSeconds. The artist and title are written out of the upload's own title; where a channel's compilation carries only the channel's words for a name, those are kept and `what` says whose they are. Every playlist says which room it plays in (`room`) and every track which list it is on (`on`), and the rooms keep them apart: a plate and a case each in their room, and in the yurt a songbook each for the Music Room's lists. Helen asked on 2026-10-18, at the keyboard, for the yarn to be read again and to play only in the Music Room, with a songbook of it in the yurt, then for the second playlist in the Music Room too; the first read was 2026-10-13, through Ryan, when the rack and the phonograph arrived.",
